# EdgeCMS AI Agent Rules (.cursorrules)

You are an expert full-stack engineer and AI coding assistant working on an EdgeCMS project.

## Core Architecture
- **Backend:** Hono REST API running on Cloudflare Workers with D1 (SQLite) and R2 (Media Storage).
- **Admin Studio:** SvelteKit dashboard with Pure Black OLED aesthetics (`#000000`, `#222222` hairline borders).
- **Public Web:** Minimalist frontend in `apps/web`.

---

## 🛠️ Schema Management (Code-First)
When the user asks you to create, update, or design content schemas/collections:
1. **Always edit `cms.config.ts` at the root of the repository.**
2. Never create schemas manually in D1 SQL or tell the user to use the UI forms unless asked.
3. The EdgeCMS API Worker **automatically detects changes to `cms.config.ts` and syncs collections to Cloudflare D1 on file save.**

### Available Field Helpers in `cms.config.ts`
Import helpers from `./packages/shared/src/builder`:
- `text(key, options)`: Single-line string (title, slug, name)
- `longtext(key, options)`: Multi-line plain text (bio, notes)
- `richtext(key, options)`: Rich HTML content (WYSIWYG blog body)
- `number(key, options)`: Numeric values (price, count, rating)
- `boolean(key, options)`: True/false toggle (in_stock, is_featured)
- `date(key, options)`: Calendar date (published_date, event_date)
- `media(key, options)`: Asset URL from Cloudflare R2 uploader (thumbnail, avatar)
- `select(key, options)`: Enum dropdown, e.g. `{ options: ['Draft', 'Review', 'Published'] }`
- `relation(key, targetSlug, options)`: Link to another collection (e.g. author, category)

### Schema Example:
```typescript
import {
  defineCollection,
  defineConfig,
  text,
  number,
  richtext,
  media,
  boolean,
  relation
} from './packages/shared/src/builder';

export const cmsConfig = defineConfig({
  collections: [
    defineCollection({
      slug: 'products',
      name: 'Products',
      description: 'E-commerce product catalog',
      icon: 'box',
      fields: [
        text('title', { label: 'Product Title', required: true }),
        number('price', { label: 'Price (USD)', required: true }),
        richtext('description', { label: 'Product Details' }),
        media('thumbnail', { label: 'Featured Image' }),
        boolean('in_stock', { label: 'In Stock' })
      ]
    })
  ]
});

export default cmsConfig;
```

---

## 📡 Frontend Fetching
To query published content in Astro/Next.js frontend:
```typescript
import { getCMSContent } from '../lib/cms';

// Fetches all published items with relational fields populated:
const products = await getCMSContent('products');
```

